  "functions": [
    "FUNC.ADDRESS"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "ADDRESS quotes sheet names resembling R1C1 axis prefixes (even R1048576C16385), omits quotes after [book], and allows signed relative R1C1 offsets",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, ADDRESS quotes sheet_text not only for A1 references, spaces, punctuation, and TRUE/FALSE, but also for any unbracketed name starting with R<1..1048576> or C<1..16384> or RC<1..16384> not followed by a dot (so R1048576C16385 and R1048576C and R1C000 are quoted, whereas R1048577C16384 is not). A workbook-prefixed sheet_text like [a]TRUE is not quoted when the book and sheet parts use identifier characters, and empty sheet_text produces an unquoted '!'. When a1 is FALSE and abs_num selects relative coordinates (abs_num 2, 3, or 4), row_num and column_num admit negative and zero offsets in (-limit+1)..limit and format zero as R or C without brackets.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0 build 20430 across w111-broad, w111-address-sheet-20260929, and w111-address-refinement-20260929 in CalcFunc-Evidence, and matched on 1,284/1,284 full-bank ADDRESS rows.",
